{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "black background pixels plus the unique non-black non-grey marker pixel",
  "transform": "copy the marker color to every black pixel with the same row parity and column parity as the marker; keep grey pixels and other black pixels unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 13-15 rows x 13-17 cols
  colors: exactly 3 — black (background), grey (obstacle), one marker color (any non-black non-grey)
  grey_pixels:
    density: 30-45% of grid
    structure: 2-5 connected blobs (8-conn), forming irregular thick clusters concentrated toward edges/corners
    border_density: 55-67% of perimeter cells are grey [observed]
    no_full_rows_or_cols: no row or column is entirely grey [observed]
  marker:
    count: exactly 1 pixel of the marker color
    placement: on a black cell with all 4 cardinal neighbors also black; Manhattan distance >= 3 to nearest grey
    must_be_in_main_open_component: the largest 4-connected non-grey region (55-85 cells for 13x13 up to ~150 for 15x17)
  open_region:
    largest_component: 55-67% fill ratio within its bounding box; spans most of the grid
  transformation:
    rule: recolor every black cell whose (row%2, col%2) matches the marker's (row%2, col%2) with the marker color
    grey_unchanged: true
    black_other_parity_unchanged: true

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size H in [13,15], W in [13,17] (odd values preferred to match eval)
    2. Place 2-4 irregular grey blobs near edges/corners using random walks or flood fills, targeting 30-45% grey coverage; ensure no row/col is fully grey
    3. Compute the largest 4-connected non-grey component; if it covers < 50% of grid, regenerate blobs
    4. Pick a random marker color from {1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9}
    5. Choose a random cell in the main open component that has all 4 neighbors also in the component and Manhattan distance >= 3 to nearest grey; place the marker
    6. Output is derived by applying the parity-fill rule (no inversion needed — input is the constructed grid)
```
